# robert-real-email-domain -- RESOLVED 2026-11-13, not just suppressed.
#
# This custom (gitignored, local-only) rule flags Robert's real personal
# email domain. A bulk exclusion for it used to live here (added 2026-10-29,
# ~815 entries) covering this repo's own then-existing, deliberate use of
# that domain as a generic illustrative placeholder -- ad_email_domain
# examples in a handful of comments/docs, and (at far greater volume) the
# fictional ad_users.json/ad_groups.json AD export dataset's synthetic
# per-user email addresses.
#
# Robert's own call, 2026-11-13, on being shown the breakdown: the real
# domain should never have been the placeholder in the first place --
# RFC 2606 (example.com/.net/.org) exists exactly for this. Fixed properly
# instead of re-ignored:
#   1. The 8 then-current, live occurrences (comments in
#      ansible/playbooks/windows_adschema/playbooks/10-ad-schema.yml,
#      benarbejde/archive/parse_tdf.py, at_have_ryggen_fri/README.md,
#      at_have_ryggen_fri/check_collection_requirements.py) were edited to
#      example.com.
#   2. The remaining ~806 were historical-only (ad_users.json/ad_groups.json
#      had already been converted to jukebox.internal at some point after
#      the TDF-to-JSON conversion, confirmed by diffing the actual flagged
#      historical commit against HEAD) -- scrubbed from the entire git
#      history via `git filter-repo --replace-text` (blob content) and
#      `--replace-message` (the one commit message that also quoted the
#      domain as illustrative text), then force-pushed.
#
# Re-scanned clean afterward: 0 robert-real-email-domain findings anywhere
# in history. The bulk exclusion block is therefore deleted entirely, not
# kept around as dead weight -- there is nothing left for it to suppress,
# and an empty-in-practice allowlist block is a worse trap for a future
# reader than no block at all. The custom rule itself stays active (in
# .gitleaks.local.toml, never committed) to catch any NEW leak the same way.
